      "id": 1,
      "text": "Catawissa was laid out in 1858 and likely named after Catawissa, Pennsylvania, whose name means \"clear water\" or \"growing fat\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catawissa%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Catawissa since 1860, supporting local farmers and loggers during the timber boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catawissa%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community grew around a Pacific Railroad depot that operated until the mid‑20th century, linking it to the St. Louis–San Francisco Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        7,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
