        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/catawissa_missouri",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "James Catholic Church, dedicated in 1913, reflects Catawissa’s strong German and Irish immigrant heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/catawissa_missouri",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Catawissa sits on the east bank of the Meramec River, about 39 miles southwest of St. Louis, and its elevation is roughly 528 feet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        27,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
